              "title": "Trace how `POST /api/v1/input` and `POST /api/v1/command` drive `TitleScreen.tscn` -> `PartyCreate.tscn` -> `Coneria.tscn`"
            }
          ],
          "quiz": [
            {
              "question": "How does the external Python Cucumber (behave) test runner deterministically inspect scene state and drive player actions inside the running Godot 4 process under Xvfb?",
              "options": [
                "By attaching a GDScript debugger over port 6007 and evaluating raw expression strings against the scene tree between physics ticks",
                "Through the autoloaded GameControlServer.gd TCP HTTP/JSON bridge on 127.0.0.1:8090 (/api/v1/state, /api/v1/input, /api/v1/command), which polls non-blocking sockets inside _process()",
                "By sending xdotool X11 keystrokes to the Xvfb display window and running Tesseract OCR on periodic ImageMagick screenshots to read dialogue text",
                "By writing input commands to a shared SQLite WAL file in /tmp that FF1MapScene.gd polls every 500ms via OS.execute()"
              ],
              "answer": "Through the autoloaded GameControlServer.gd TCP HTTP/JSON bridge on 127.0.0.1:8090 (/api/v1/state, /api/v1/input, /api/v1/command), which polls non-blocking sockets inside _process()",
              "explanation": "GameControlServer.gd runs as a Godot autoload singleton listening on 127.0.0.1:8090 using TCPServer inside _process(). Unlike flaky X11 keystrokes or OCR, it provides exact JSON state snapshots (hero tile coordinates, active dialogue text, battle HP, party gold) and frame-accurate InputEventAction injection."
            },
            {
              "question": "After re-rendering maps/temple_of_fiends.png on disk with the corrected inside-room palette, why did Godot 4’s --write-movie recording still show the old texture until godot4 --headless --path <project> --import was executed?",
              "options": [
                "Because GDScript preloads all PNG files into the Linux kernel page cache when Xvfb starts and requires a SIGHUP signal to flush /dev/shm",
                "Because Godot’s GL Compatibility renderer caches textures inside ~/.cache/mesa_shader_cache until --import clears the OpenGL context",
                "Because Godot 4 runtime scenes load pre-imported .godot/imported/*.ctex compressed texture caches referenced by .import sidecars rather than decoding raw res://assets/maps/*.png files on the fly",
                "Because build_ff1_godot_game.py embeds base64-encoded PNG strings directly inside .tscn scene files during generation"
              ],
              "answer": "Because Godot 4 runtime scenes load pre-imported .godot/imported/*.ctex compressed texture caches referenced by .import sidecars rather than decoding raw res://assets/maps/*.png files on the fly",
              "explanation": "When load(\"res://assets/maps/temple_of_fiends.png\") is called in Godot 4, the ResourceLoader reads the .import file and loads the binary .ctex artifact from .godot/imported/. Running godot4 --headless --path <project> --import rebuilds the .ctex cache whenever an underlying PNG is updated on disk."
            },
            {
              "question": "When jrpg-parser.js publish --out ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes --to ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public prepares a Knowledge Graph for public redistribution, what transformation does it perform alongside clean-room art from jrpg-generate-art?",
              "options": [
                "It merges the raw VGMaps PNGs and NSF audio archives directly into a single monolithic .pck file for GitHub Releases",
                "It compiles the JSON-LD graph into an encrypted WebAssembly binary so players cannot inspect monster stats in the browser",
                "It replaces all D&D-inspired monster names with randomized UUIDs and scales all stats by 1.5x",
                "It strips local file paths, SHA-256 source hashes, and verbatim guide quotes from every node while preserving the clean-room schema facts, formulas, and generated art references"
              ],
              "answer": "It strips local file paths, SHA-256 source hashes, and verbatim guide quotes from every node while preserving the clean-room schema facts, formulas, and generated art references",
              "explanation": "During parsing, ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes records provenance (source filenames, hashes, and verbatim quotes used by the anti-hallucination gate). Running publish writes a clean graph that strips copyrighted verbatim prose and local scrape paths while keeping the clean-room structural facts and generated art."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "mod-06-cucumber-playthrough-and-visual-debugging",
          "title": "Module 6: Running the Cucumber (behave) Video Playthroughs & Fixing Visual Bugs from Frames",
          "durationMinutes": 25,
          "overview": "Run behave tests/e2e/features --no-capture inside /home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game to record the 3 MP4 playthrough videos under Xvfb :98, and walk through the exact ffmpeg frame-extraction loop we used to spot and fix the Coneria tree-spawn bug and the Temple of Fiends teal-box treasure chest bug.",
          "lessonHtml": "\n        <div class=\"lesson-section\">\n          <h4 class=\"lesson-subtitle\">1. Recording Deterministic 60 FPS Playthrough Videos with <code>behave</code> and <code>--write-movie</code></h4>\n          <p class=\"lesson-text\">\n            In <code>/home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game/tests/e2e/</code>, <code>environment.py</code> starts a virtual X11 display (<code>Xvfb :98 -screen 0 768x720x24</code>) before the test run. For each Gherkin scenario in <code>tests/e2e/features/</code>, it launches <code>godot4</code> with <code>--write-movie &lt;scenario&gt;.avi --fixed-fps 60</code>, executes the Gherkin steps against <code>http://127.0.0.1:8090</code>, saves the final JSON state from <code>/api/v1/state</code> into <code>tests/e2e/reports/gamestate_&lt;scenario&gt;.json</code>, and transcodes the AVI into an H.264 MP4 in <code>tests/e2e/reports/videos/</code>.\n          </p>\n          <pre class=\"code-snippet\"><code># Run all 3 Gherkin features and record MP4 proof-of-work videos:\ncd /home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game\nbehave tests/e2e/features --no-capture\n\n# Generated MP4 videos in /home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game/tests/e2e/reports/videos/:\n# 1. start_a_new_game_from_title_screen_create_4_light_warriors_and_enter_coneria.mp4\n# 2. speak_to_coneria_townsfolk_and_the_king_of_coneria_in_the_throne_room.mp4\n# 3. open_a_treasure_chest_in_the_temple_of_fiends_and_defeat_garland.mp4</code></pre>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"lesson-section\">\n          <h4 class=\"lesson-subtitle\">2. Why Green Gherkin Assertions Were Not Enough: Fixing the Two Visual Bugs</h4>\n          <p class=\"lesson-text\">\n            When we first ran <code>behave tests/e2e/features</code>, all 3 scenarios and all 29 Gherkin steps passed. If we had only checked the exit code (<code>0</code>) or the JSON state assertions, we would have stopped there. Watching the recorded MP4 videos—and extracting PNG frames with <code>ffmpeg -frames:v 1</code>—exposed two visual bugs right away:\n          </p>\n          <p class=\"lesson-text\">\n            <strong>Visual Bug 1 — The Hero Ended Scenario 1 Stuck in a Tree:</strong> In <code>start_a_new_game_from_title_screen_create_4_light_warriors_and_enter_coneria.mp4</code>, the Gherkin assertion only checked that the current scene name was <code>\"Coneria\"</code>. Because we had initially set <code>spawn_tile = Vector2i(15, 22)</code>, the hero spawned on top of the left border tree column (<code>x=15</code>, <code>tileId=14</code>) instead of the central brick entrance street (<code>x=16</code>, <code>tileId=16</code>). We fixed <code>PartyCreate.gd</code> and <code>FF1MapScene.gd</code> to spawn at <code>Vector2i(16, 21)</code> on the brick road and added <code>When the hero moves up 3 tiles</code> to walk cleanly up the street to <code>(16, 18)</code>.\n          </p>\n          <p class=\"lesson-text\">\n            <strong>Visual Bug 2 — Treasure Chests Rendered as Solid Teal Boxes in Scenario 3:</strong> In <code>open_a_treasure_chest_in_the_temple_of_fiends_and_defeat_garland.mp4</code>, opening chest <code>(3, 3)</code> added <code>Heal Potion</code> to the party's inventory and passed the Gherkin assertion, but visually the chests at <code>(2, 3)</code> and <code>(3, 3)</code> were solid teal squares! Two mistakes had combined:\n          </p>\n          <pre class=\"code-snippet\"><code># Why chest tiles (2,3) and (3,3) looked like solid teal boxes before our fix:\n# 1. temple_of_fiends.png had been rendered with Outside-Room Palette 0 ([0x0F, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30] solid white)\n# 2. FF1MapScene.gd drew a semi-transparent ColorRect (_chest_markers) on top of every chest coordinate,\n#    which alpha-blended against the solid white tile into a flat teal box!\n\n# How we verified the fix from the re-recorded MP4 videos using FFmpeg:\nffmpeg -y -sseof -0.3 -i tests/e2e/reports/videos/start_a_new_game_from_title_screen_create_4_light_warriors_and_enter_coneria.mp4 \\\n  -frames:v 1 /tmp/verify_coneria.png\nffmpeg -y -ss 0.5 -i tests/e2e/reports/videos/open_a_treasure_chest_in_the_temple_of_fiends_and_defeat_garland.mp4 \\\n  -frames:v 1 /tmp/verify_chest.png</code></pre>\n          <p class=\"lesson-text\">\n            After re-rendering <code>temple_of_fiends.png</code> with Inside-Room Palette 0 (<code>+0x20</code>: <code>[0x0F, 0x10, 0x17, 0x0F]</code>), removing the <code>_chest_markers</code> <code>ColorRect</code> overlay from <code>FF1MapScene.gd</code> (replacing it with a dark open-chest interior graphic drawn only <em>after</em> a chest is opened), running <code>godot4 --headless --path /home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game --import</code>, and re-running <code>behave</code>, both extracted verification frames showed the hero standing cleanly on the Coneria brick road at <code>(16, 18)</code> and the authentic wooden-and-silver NES treasure chests at <code>(2, 3)</code> and <code>(3, 3)</code>.\n          </p>\n          <div class=\"doc-figure\">\n            <img src=\"/assets/elearning/jrpg-kgraph/jrpg-godot-cucumber-playthrough-harness.png\" alt=\"Stage 3: Godot 4 Scene Engine, HTTP Control Bridge and Xvfb Cucumber Video Proof-of-Work\" class=\"doc-img\" onclick=\"openLightbox(this.src, this.alt)\">\n            <div class=\"doc-caption\">Figure 3.1: Stage 3 verification loop — Cucumber behave runner, Port 8090 HTTP control bridge, headless Xvfb Godot 4 Movie Maker recording, and FFmpeg frame extraction.</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      ",
          "labSteps": [
            "Run `behave tests/e2e/features --no-capture` in `/home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game` and verify all 3 features, 3 scenarios, and 29 steps pass",
            "Extract the title and final frames of Scenario 1 (`start_a_new_game_...mp4`) with `ffmpeg` and verify the hero stands on the brick street at `(16, 18)`",
            "Inspect Scenario 2 (`speak_to_coneria_townsfolk_and_the_king_of_coneria_in_the_throne_room.mp4`) and its `gamestate_*.json` report",
            "Extract frame `0.5s` and the final battle frame of Scenario 3 (`open_a_treasure_chest_...mp4`) to verify the silver-and-brown NES chests at `(2, 3)` and `(3, 3)` and Garland’s defeat"
          ],
          "labDetails": [
            {
              "description": "Run the Cucumber (`behave`) E2E suite inside `/home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game` to execute all 3 scenarios inside `Xvfb :98` and record fresh MP4 videos.",
              "code": "cd /home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game\nbehave tests/e2e/features --no-capture\nls -lh tests/e2e/reports/videos/",
              "expected": "`behave` outputs `3 features passed, 0 failed`, `3 scenarios passed, 0 failed`, and `29 steps passed, 0 failed`, and writes all 3 `.mp4` videos into `tests/e2e/reports/videos/`.",
              "image": "/assets/elearning/jrpg-kgraph/labs/lab-m6-s1-behave-test-run.png",
              "imageAlt": "Terminal output of behave tests/e2e/features showing 3 features, 3 scenarios, and 29 steps passing",
              "caption": "Lab 6.1: Running behave tests/e2e/features --no-capture and confirming all 3 scenarios and 29 Gherkin steps pass.",
              "title": "Run `behave tests/e2e/features --no-capture` in `/home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game` and verify all 3 features, 3 scenarios, and 29 steps pass"
            },
            {
              "description": "Use `ffmpeg` to extract the opening title frame (`-ss 0.2`) and final Coneria frame (`-sseof -0.3`) from `start_a_new_game_from_title_screen_create_4_light_warriors_and_enter_coneria.mp4` and check the saved `hero_position`.",
              "code": "cd /home/ndipiazza/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game\nffmpeg -y -sseof -0.3 -i tests/e2e/reports/videos/start_a_new_game_from_title_screen_create_4_light_warriors_and_enter_coneria.mp4 \\\n  -frames:v 1 /tmp/verify_coneria.png\njq '{scene: .scene_shown.name, hero_position, gold: .game_state.gold}' \\\n  tests/e2e/reports/gamestate_start_a_new_game_from_title_screen_create_4_light_warriors_and_enter_coneria.json",
              "expected": "The extracted frame `/tmp/verify_coneria.png` shows the hero standing on the central brick entrance path at `(16, 18)` in Coneria (no longer stuck in the tree at `(15, 22)`), and `jq` confirms `{\"x\": 16, \"y\": 18, \"facing\": \"up\"}`.",
              "image": "/assets/elearning/jrpg-kgraph/labs/lab-m6-s2-scenario1-coneria-fix.png",
              "imageAlt": "Extracted video frames from Scenario 1 showing the NES Title Screen and the hero standing on the Coneria brick road at (16, 18)",
              "caption": "Lab 6.2: Scenario 1 extracted frames — from TitleScreen.tscn to standing cleanly on Coneria’s central brick road at (16, 18).",
