              "title": "Inspect `/home/ndipiazza/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes/parsed.json` with `jq` to review the 5 cross-source equipment conflicts and the Elfland shop mismatch"
            },
            {
              "description": "Compare what StrategyWiki’s bestiary table provides (`hp`, `xp`, `gold`) against the full 20-byte NES monster record (`attack`, `accuracy`, `hits`, `critRate`, `defense`, `evade`, `magicDefense`, `morale`, `ai`) required to run battles.",
              "code": "jq '.enemies[] | select(.name == \"IMP\") | {name, hp, xp, gold, attack, accuracy, hits, critRate, defense, evade, magicDefense, morale}' \\\n  /home/ndipiazza/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes/parsed.json",
              "expected": "Every combat property (`attack: 4, accuracy: 2, hits: 1, critRate: 1, defense: 4, evade: 6, magicDefense: 16, morale: 106`) is populated once the ROM tables are merged, whereas a wiki-only scrape leaves all eight combat stats `null`.",
              "image": "/assets/elearning/jrpg-kgraph/labs/lab-m2-s3-gap-audit-comparison.png",
              "imageAlt": "Side-by-side comparison of Wiki-only enemy node vs full NES ROM enemy node and the 5 gameplay blockers",
              "caption": "Lab 2.3: Side-by-side comparison of a Wiki-only enemy record (which blocks combat) versus the complete NES ROM combat struct.",
              "title": "Compare a Wiki-only `robos:JRPGEnemy` node (`HP, XP, Gold` only) against the full NES combat stat structure required to resolve a turn of battle"
            },
            {
              "description": "Run the `robos-jrpg-parser` unit test suite to verify that file classification, edition filtering, table parsing, verbatim quote verification, JSON-LD generation, and clean-room publishing all pass.",
