          "quiz": [
            {
              "question": "When rendering Temple of Fiends (Map 12) from the 6502 ROM’s lut_SMPalettes table ($A000 in bank_00.dat, 48 bytes per map), why did reading bytes 0..15 cause the treasure chests at (2, 3) and (3, 3) to render as blank white squares?",
              "options": [
                "Because Temple of Fiends uses bank-switched CHR-RAM animation frames that overwrite tile 0x3F only after the player defeats Garland in the central chamber",
                "Because treasure chests on the NES are rendered via OAM sprite slots (bytes 16..31) rather than background nametable metatiles, so background Palette 0 contains no chest colors",
                "Because bytes 0..3 represent Outside-Room Palette 0 ([0x0F, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30]), which intentionally paints indoor room metatiles and chests in solid white (0x30) until the player steps inside and triggers the Inside-Room palette at offset +0x20 ([0x0F, 0x10, 0x17, 0x0F])",
                "Because bytes 0..15 store the 4-color grayscale PPU attribute mask rather than NES master palette indices, requiring a bitwise XOR with 0x3F before RGB lookup"
              ],
              "answer": "Because bytes 0..3 represent Outside-Room Palette 0 ([0x0F, 0x30, 0x30, 0x30]), which intentionally paints indoor room metatiles and chests in solid white (0x30) until the player steps inside and triggers the Inside-Room palette at offset +0x20 ([0x0F, 0x10, 0x17, 0x0F])",
              "explanation": "Each map entry in lut_SMPalettes is 0x30 (48) bytes: 0x00..0x0F are the 4 outside-room background palettes, 0x10..0x1F are sprite palettes, and 0x20..0x2F are the 4 inside-room background palettes. Replacing Palette 0 with in_room_pal[0:4] ([0x0F, 0x10, 0x17, 0x0F]) restores the black, silver, and brown chest pixels."
            },
